  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Examples of transverse waves are:\n\n  - Electromagnetic waves e.g. radio, visible light, UV\n  - Vibrations on a guitar string\n  - Waves on a rope or slinky"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Transverse waves can be *polarised*"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "variant": "exam-tip",
   "label": "Exam Hint",
   "md": "Questions about transverse waves typically start by asking for a definition, so be ready with a statement about **vibrations **or **oscillations **being perpendicular to the travel of the wave."
